   "notes": "Low-evidence placeholder of the same class as hejaz-tribes. Chaldean and Aramean tribes (Bit-Yakin, the Gambulu) lived in the marshes and are attested in Neo-Assyrian and Neo-Babylonian sources; the Hellenistic record for 270 names no ruler, seat or event, and Seleucid rule reached the marsh only nominally. Characene did not exist: Hyspaosines founded it in 141 BCE, after Antiochus IV refounded the Tigris-mouth city as Antiochia about 166-165. Fold into seleucid-empire if the lead wants no tribal actor here. Every settlement is a placeholder.",
