   "ruler": null,
   "notes": "Xenophon's Arabs on the Euphrates (Anabasis 1.5) and Strabo's Scenitae (16.1.27) are the only Greek names; both are recalled, not re-read. The tribal names Tayy, Kalb and the rest are later or from Islamic sources and are not used; Rhambaei is a name from Gedrosia in Arrian, not Arabia. The ring reaches from the Wadi Hauran across the Hamad to the Euphrates' west bank as far as Kuwait's desert and abuts qedar at the Sirhan. Kuwait's mainland coast is in this ring: nothing Seleucid is known there except the fort on Failaka (Ikaros). Ain al-Tamr is an old oasis (Neo-Babylonian Shithatha); Rutba, Sulman and the Hauran camp are marked places only. Hira is a 3rd-century CE city: not used.",
