    "name": "Seleucus, eldest son of Antiochus I",
    "title": "Viceroy of the upper satrapies",
    "confidence": "medium"
   },
   "notes": "Iraq is the default holder, in three parts: Babylonia and the alluvium from Sippar to Ur; the Assyrian edge (Nineveh, Arbela, Ashur, Kirkuk) inside the Anatolian file's Seleucid ring; the Jazira with Nisibis. The settlements are in seleucidCities, not here. The west edge follows the Euphrates' west bank; the Arab ring and the marsh ring take precedence. The east edge abuts the Zagros Seleucid ring of the Levant/Iran file (Susiana, Media) and stops short of Atropatene. Zagros hill peoples (Cossaeans, Uxians) and Elymais have no independent polity in 270 (no king of Elymais before about 147) and stay inside the Seleucid rings of the Iran file.",
